---
module: python-tui-app-boilerplate
func_id: ctrl-d-exit
---

***conformance tests***

# exit-on-ctrl-d
Pressing ctrl+d while :App: is running terminates it gracefully.
- :App: is running in a pseudo-terminal with an empty :TaskList:.
- ctrl+d is sent to the terminal.
- The process exits with status 0 within 5 seconds and the terminal is restored to its normal state.

# ctrl-d-ignored-in-modal
Scenario: ctrl+d is ignored while a modal input has focus
  Given :App: is running in a pseudo-terminal
  And the add-task modal is open with the name field focused
  When ctrl+d is sent to the terminal
  Then :App: keeps running
  And the modal stays open

# ctrl-d-exits-with-populated-list
description: Pressing ctrl+d exits :App: gracefully even when :TaskList: contains items.
given:
  - :App: is running in a pseudo-terminal
  - :TaskList: contains two tasks
when:
  - ctrl+d is sent to the terminal
then:
  - the process exits with status 0 within 5 seconds
  - the terminal is restored to its normal state

***acceptance tests***
